# Core Distro Chat Latency — Read-Only Diagnosis

**Date:** 2026-10-18 (UTC)  
**Scope:** Repeated live staging probes and isolation assessment. No production, DNS, application, proxy, or service configuration was changed. No request was sent to `llm.hd2.ai` or another HD2-internal service.

## Finding

**The reported 847 ms is not confirmed as a current TTFT.** Repeated requests to the client staging chat route did not yield a token or a valid chat response: all three synthetic POSTs returned HTTP 401 `Invalid request` after 802.6–823.4 ms. These are failed-request response times, not TTFT. Therefore there is no valid current TTFT sample to compare with the 500 ms SLA, and it is not justified to claim either that 847 ms holds or that it has drifted.

The current evidence points first to a **staging chat-route / embed-request validity failure**, not a measured slow model. The stage's `/llm/chat/` route still returns a bare nginx 404. A request at `/api/embed/<embed-id>/stream-chat` reaches an Express response but is rejected as invalid. The client widget's actual live embed ID/configuration and backend/provider trace were not established. The request path cannot be attributed to a specific downstream service timing from these external observations alone.

## Measurements

Probe vantage: `brandon-compute`; timestamp from host: `2026-10-18T01:37:35Z`. `staging.core-distro.com` resolved locally to `45.90.220.156`. All timings below are curl wall-clock fields; `time_starttransfer` is response first-byte timing, **not chat TTFT**.

